Findings: A small patch-like slightly low-density lesion with clear borders is seen in segment 8 of the liver, measuring 4mm 	imes 8mm; obvious enhancement is seen in the arterial phase of the enhanced scan, and the density is equal in the venous phase and delayed phase; multiple circular low-density non-enhanced areas are seen in the liver parenchyma, with the largest one located in segment 5 of the liver (approximately 16mm 	imes 13mm). No dilation of the intrahepatic or extrahepatic bile ducts is seen. No abnormalities are observed in the gallbladder. A nodule of uniform enhancement measuring approximately 6mm in diameter is seen in the adrenal gland on the left side. A spot-like high dense lesion is seen in the renal sinus on the right side. Two small cystic low-density non-enhanced lesions, with the largest one measuring approximately 4mm in diameter, are seen in the lower pole of the left kidney. No abnormalities are observed in the pancreas, spleen, and adrenal gland on the right side.
No abnormalities are observed in the uterus and bilateral adnexal areas. No abnormalities are observed in the bladder. No enlarged lymph nodes are seen in the abdominal cavity or retroperitoneum. No definite signs of fluid accumulation are observed in the pelvis or abdominal cavity.

Impression: 1. A hemangioma in liver segment 8;
2. multiple hepatic cysts.
3. a small kidney stone on the right side;
4. small cysts in the left kidney.
5. A hyperplastic nodule in the adrenal gland on the left side;

Findings: The appendix is thickened, with a diameter of approximately 10mm, and the surrounding fat planes are slightly indistinct. The liver, gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, bilateral adrenal glands, and kidneys appear normal. There is no dilation of the intrahepatic or extrahepatic bile ducts. No definite enlarged lymph nodes are observed in the abdominal or pelvic cavity.
A vaguely demarcated cystic lesion measuring approximately 20mm×16mm with slightly lower density, with an approximate CT attenuation value of 13 Hounsfield units, is faintly visible in the left adnexal area. A small amount of fluid is observed in the Douglas pouch. No abnormalities are found in the bladder, uterus, or right adnexal area.

Impression: 1. Appendicitis;
2. minimal fluid accumulation in the pelvic cavity;
3. follicle in the left adnexa possible.
